ength](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_array_new_length.html \"cpp/memory/new/bad array new length\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [align\\_val\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/new/align_val_t.html \"cpp/memory/new/align val t\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [destroying\\_delete\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/new/destroying_delete_t.html \"cpp/memory/new/destroying delete t\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [launder](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/launder.html \"cpp/utility/launder\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [Smart pointers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory.html#Smart_pointers \"cpp/memory\") |\n| [unique\\_ptr](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr.html \"cpp/memory/unique ptr\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [shared\\_ptr](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr.html \"cpp/memory/shared ptr\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [weak\\_ptr](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/weak_ptr.html \"cpp/memory/weak ptr\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [auto\\_ptr](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/auto_ptr.html \"cpp/memory/auto ptr\")<br>(until C++17\\*) |\n| [owner\\_less](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/owner_less.html \"cpp/memory/owner less\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [owner\\_less<void>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/owner_less_void.html \"cpp/memory/owner less void\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [owner\\_hash](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/owner_hash.html \"cpp/memory/owner hash\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [owner\\_equal](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/owner_equal.html \"cpp/memory/owner equal\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [enable\\_shared\\_from\\_this](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/enable_shared_from_this.html \"cpp/memory/enable shared from this\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [bad\\_weak\\_ptr](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/bad_weak_ptr.html \"cpp/memory/bad weak ptr\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [default\\_delete](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/default_delete.html \"cpp/memory/default delete\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [out\\_ptr\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/out_ptr_t.html \"cpp/memory/out ptr t\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [inout\\_ptr\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/inout_ptr_t.html \"cpp/memory/inout ptr t\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [Miscellaneous](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory.html#Miscellaneous \"cpp/memory\") |\n| [pointer\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/pointer_traits.html \"cpp/memory/pointer traits\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [to\\_address](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/to_address.html \"cpp/memory/to address\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [addressof](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/addressof.html \"cpp/memory/addressof\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [align](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/align.html \"cpp/memory/align\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [assume\\_aligned](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/assume_aligned.html \"cpp/memory/assume aligned\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [is\\_sufficiently\\_aligned](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/is_sufficiently_aligned.html \"cpp/memory/is sufficiently aligned\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [C Library](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/c.html \"cpp/memory/c\") |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [malloc](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/c/malloc.html \"cpp/memory/c/malloc\") |\n| [calloc](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/c/calloc.html \"cpp/memory/c/calloc\") |\n| [realloc](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/c/realloc.html \"cpp/memory/c/realloc\") | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [free](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/c/free.html \"cpp/memory/c/free\") |\n| [aligned\\_alloc](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/c/aligned_alloc.html \"cpp/memory/c/aligned alloc\")<br>(C++17) |\n|  | | |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n**`std::allocator`**\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| Member functions |\n| [allocator::allocator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocator.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/allocator\") |\n| [allocator::~allocator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/~allocator.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/~allocator\") |\n| [allocator::address](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/address.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/address\")<br>(until C++20) |\n| [allocator::allocate](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocate.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/allocate\") |\n| [allocator::allocate\\_at\\_least](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocate_at_least.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/allocate at least\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [allocator::deallocate](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/deallocate.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/deallocate\") |\n| [allocator::max\\_size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/max_size.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/max size\")<br>(until C++20) |\n| [allocator::construct](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/construct.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/construct\")<br>(until C++20) |\n| [allocator::destroy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/destroy.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/destroy\")<br>(until C++20) |\n| Non-member functions |\n| [operator==operator!=](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/operator cmp\")<br>(until C++20) |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<memory>` |  |  |\n| template<class T ><br>struct allocator; | (1) |  |\n| template<><br>struct allocator<void>; | (2) | (deprecated in C++17)<br>(removed in C++20) |\n|  |  |  |\n\nThe `std::allocator` class template is the default [Allocator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/Allocator.html \"cpp/named req/Allocator\") used by all standard library containers if no user-specified allocator is provided. The default allocator is stateless, that is, all instances of the given allocator are interchangeable, compare equal and can deallocate memory allocated by any other instance of the same allocator type.\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| The explicit specialization for void lacks the member typedefs `reference`, `const_reference`, `size_type` and `difference_type`. This specialization declares no member functions. | (until C++20) |\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| The default allocator satisfies [allocator completeness requirements](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/Allocator.html#Allocator_completeness_requirements \"cpp/named req/Allocator\"). | (since C++17) |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| ## Contents<br>- [1Member types](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#Member_types)<br>- [2Member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#Member_functions)<br>- [3Non-member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#Non-member_functions)<br>- [4Notes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#Notes)<br>- [5Example](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#Example)<br>- [6Defect reports](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#Defect_reports)<br>- [7See also](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator.html#See_also) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Member types\")\\]Member types\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Type | Definition |\n| `value_type` | `T` |\n| `pointer`(deprecated in C++17)(removed in C++20) | `T*` |\n| `const_pointer`(deprecated in C++17)(removed in C++20) | const T\\* |\n| `reference`(deprecated in C++17)(removed in C++20) | `T&` |\n| `const_reference`(deprecated in C++17)(removed in C++20) | const T& |\n| `size_type` | [std::size\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t.html \"cpp/types/size t\") |\n| `difference_type` | [std::ptrdiff\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/ptrdiff_t.html \"cpp/types/ptrdiff t\") |\n| `propagate_on_container_move_assignment`(C++11) | [std::true\\_type](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/integral_constant.html \"cpp/types/integral constant\") |\n| `rebind`(deprecated in C++17)(removed in C++20) | template<class U ><br>struct rebind<br>{<br>typedef allocator<U> other;<br>}; |\n| `is_always_equal`(C++11)(deprecated in C++23)(removed in C++26) | [std::true\\_type](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/integral_constant.html \"cpp/types/integral constant\") |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Member functions\")\\]Member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [(constructor)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocator.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/allocator\") | creates a new allocator instance <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_allocator&action=edit) |\n| [(destructor)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/~allocator.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/~allocator\") | destructs an allocator instance <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_%7Eallocator&action=edit) |\n| [address](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/address.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/address\")<br>(until C++20) | obtains the address of an object, even if operator& is overloaded <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_address&action=edit) |\n| [allocate](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocate.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/allocate\") | allocates uninitialized storage <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_allocate&action=edit) |\n| [allocate\\_at\\_least](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocate_at_least.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/allocate at least\")<br>(C++23) | allocates uninitialized storage at least as large as requested size <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_allocate_at_least&action=edit) |\n| [deallocate](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/deallocate.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/deallocate\") | deallocates storage <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_deallocate&action=edit) |\n| [max\\_size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/max_size.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/max size\")<br>(until C++20) | returns the largest supported allocation size <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_max_size&action=edit) |\n| [construct](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/construct.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/construct\")<br>(until C++20) | constructs an object in allocated storage <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_construct&action=edit) |\n| [destroy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/destroy.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/destroy\")<br>(until C++20) | destructs an object in allocated storage <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_destroy&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: Non-member functions\")\\]Non-member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [operator==operator!=](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/memory/allocator/operator cmp\")<br>(removed in C++20) | compares two allocator instances <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/allocator/dsc_operator_cmp&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=4 \"Edit section: Notes\")\\]Notes\n\nThe member template class `rebind` provides a way to obtain an allocator for a different type. For example, [std::list](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/list.html) <T, A> allocates nodes of some internal type `Node<T>`, using the allocator `A::rebind<Node<T>>::other`(until C++11)[std::allocator\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits.html) <A>::rebind\\_alloc<Node<T>>, which is implemented in terms of `A::rebind<Node<T>>::other` if A is an `std::allocator`(since C++11).\n\nMember type `is_always_equal` is deprecated via [LWG issue 3170](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3170), because it makes custom allocators derived from `std::allocator` treated as always equal by default. [std::allocator\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits.html) <std::allocator<T>>::is\\_always\\_equal is not deprecated and its member constant `value` is true for any `T`.\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=5 \"Edit section: Example\")\\]Example\n\nRun this code\n\n```\n#include <iostream>\n#include <memory>\n#include <string>\n\nint main()\n{\n    // default allocator for ints\n    std::allocator<int> alloc1;\n\n    // demonstrating the few directly usable members\n    static_assert(std::is_same_v<int, decltype(alloc1)::value_type>);\n    int* p1 = alloc1.allocate(1); // space for one int\n    alloc1.deallocate(p1, 1);     // and it is gone\n\n    // Even those can be used through traits though, so no need\n    using traits_t1 = std::allocator_traits<decltype(alloc1)>; // The matching trait\n    p1 = traits_t1::allocate(alloc1, 1);\n    traits_t1::construct(alloc1, p1, 7);  // construct the int\n    std::cout << *p1 << '\\n';\n    traits_t1::deallocate(alloc1, p1, 1); // deallocate space for one int\n\n    // default allocator for strings\n    std::allocator<std::string> alloc2;\n    // matching traits\n    using traits_t2 = std::allocator_traits<decltype(alloc2)>;\n\n    // Rebinding the allocator using the trait for strings gets the same type\n    traits_t2::rebind_alloc<std::string> alloc_ = alloc2;\n\n    std::string* p2 = traits_t2::allocate(alloc2, 2); // space for 2 strings\n\n    traits_t2::construct(alloc2, p2, \"foo\");\n    traits_t2::construct(alloc2, p2 + 1, \"bar\");\n\n    std::cout << p2[0] << ' ' << p2[1] << '\\n';\n\n    traits_t2::destroy(alloc2, p2 + 1);\n    traits_t2::destroy(alloc2, p2);\n    traits_t2::deallocate(alloc2, p2, 2);\n}\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n7\nfoo bar\n```\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=6 \"Edit section: Defect reports\")\\]Defect reports\n\nThe following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n\n| DR | Applied to | Behavior as published | Correct behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [LWG 2103](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2103) | C++11 | redundant comparison between `allocator` might be required | `propagate_on_container_move_assignment` provided |\n| [LWG 2108](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2108) | C++11 | there was no way to show `allocator` is stateless | `is_always_equal` provided |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=edit&section=7 \"Edit section: See also\")\\]See also\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [allocator\\_traits](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits.html \"cpp/memory/allocator traits\")<br>(C++11) | provides information about allocator types <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/dsc_allocator_traits&action=edit) |\n| [scoped\\_allocator\\_adaptor](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/scoped_allocator_adaptor.html \"cpp/memory/scoped allocator adaptor\")<br>(C++11) | implements multi-level allocator for multi-level containers <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/dsc_scoped_allocator_adaptor&action=edit) |\n| [uses\\_allocator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/uses_allocator.html \"cpp/memory/uses allocator\")<br>(C++11) | checks if the specified type supports uses-allocator construction <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/memory/dsc_uses_allocator&action=edit) |\n\nRetrieved from \" [https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&oldid=163381](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&oldid=163381)\"\n\n##### Navigation\n\n- [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n- [Recent changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n- [FAQ](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html)\n- [Offline version](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AArchives.html)\n\n##### Toolbox\n\n- [What links here](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:WhatLinksHere/cpp/memory/allocator \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n- [Related changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChangesLinked/cpp/memory/allocator \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n- [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n- [Special pages](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n- [Printable version](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&printable=yes \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n- [Permanent link](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&oldid=163381 \"Permanent link to this revision of the page\")\n- [Page information](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/memory/allocator&action=info)\n\n- In other languages\n\n- [Deutsch](http://de.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [Espa\u00f1ol](http://es.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [Fran\u00e7ais](http://fr.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [Italiano](http://it.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e](http://ja.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [Portugu\u00eas](http://pt.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439](http://ru.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n- [\u4e2d\u6587](http://zh.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator \"cpp/memory/allocator\")\n\n- This page was last modified on 22 November 2023, at 09:49.\n\n- [Privacy policy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253APrivacy_policy.html \"Cppreference:Privacy policy\")\n- [About cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html \"Cppreference:About\")\n- [Disclaimers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AGeneral_disclaimer.html \"Cppreference:General disclaimer\")\n\n- [![Powered by MediaWiki](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/skins/common/images/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png)](https://www.mediawiki.org/)[![Powered by GeSHi](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/2/2b/powered_by_geshi_88x31.png)](http://qbnz.com/highlighter/)[![Hosted by Tiger Technologies](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/9/94/powered_by_tigertech_88x31.png)](http://www.tigertech.net/referral/cppreference.com)",
